      "writtenOn": "2022-07-09T14:21:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good call. I built some more tests to verify these ideas and found a bug after all.\n\n- With optimization on, any call to main() is either recursive (error) or in a dead function (dead-stripped) so it doesn\u0027t matter.\n- With optimization off, we still do recursion checks (as it\u0027s a matter of correctness), but not dead-function elimination (considered an optimization). This means a dead call to main() can be allowed to pass through to the backend. In that case, we build a messed-up shader (pipeline-stage generator fails to rename `main`)\n\nWe\u0027ve now crossed the \"if it doesn\u0027t work correctly\" threshold so we can reevaluate. :) The easiest fix is probably to reject calls to main in FunctionCall::Convert. I can give that a go.",
      "parentUuid": "0e617e2c_9a57187d",
